soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: the msgbox FIFOs of the old core are read off before a restart

A word in the msgbox is a bare message type; its payload is in the
shared region that firmware_reset() rebuilds. Whatever the old core left
in the two FIFOs between the ARM and the MIPS outlives that rebuild.
After the standby park the MIPS sat in reset with the FIFO toward it as
it was, and a halted firmware drains nothing either. A stale CALL_ACK on
the MIPS -> ARM side would wake the first caller after the restart before
its real answer. A doorbell on the ARM -> MIPS side would reach the new
firmware before its own init (KD-1 step 2, L6 in the reload plan).

firmware_reset() now reads both FIFOs off, with the core held in reset
and before the region is rebuilt, at most a full FIFO (8 words) each,
and delivers none of the words. One info line gives both counts before,
the words read and what is left. Nothing is read when a count is 0.

The MIPS -> ARM side is read the way the receive path always reads it.
The ARM -> MIPS side is read at the doorbell address, where the MIPS
reads it. That a read from the ARM pops that FIFO is not measured, and
the restarts of 08.10.2026 did not log either count, so how often there
is anything to read is not known. The line says it.

Compiled out of tree against the R1 kernel with W=1, no new warning. Not
measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm.h
@@ -786,6 +786,7 @@ const char *cpu_comm_msgbox_bank_name(int index);
 bool cpu_comm_msgbox_owns_bank(int bank);
 int  cpu_comm_msgbox_start_polling(void *callback);
 void cpu_comm_msgbox_free_irq(void);
+void cpu_comm_msgbox_flush_mips(void);	/* before a restart, core held */
 void cpu_comm_msgbox_probe_start(void);	/* legacy stub */
 void cpu_comm_msgbox_probe_stop(void);	/* legacy stub */
 
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -1337,6 +1337,8 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_reset(void)
 	cpu_comm_shmem_adopted = false;
 	/* The boot's assumption was about the old core; start() sets it again. */
 	WRITE_ONCE(mips_app_ready_assumed, 0);
+	/* What the old core left in the msgbox, before the region is new. */
+	cpu_comm_msgbox_flush_mips();
 	ret = InitCommMem(2);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
@@ -523,6 +523,46 @@ void cpu_comm_msgbox_free_irq(void)
 	msgbox_rx_callback = NULL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Before a restart, with the coprocessor held in reset: whatever is still in
+ * the two FIFOs between this core and the MIPS belongs to the firmware that
+ * is gone. A word is a bare message type (see cpu_comm_msgbox_drain()) whose
+ * payload lives in the shared region about to be rebuilt: a stale CALL_ACK
+ * from the MIPS would wake the first caller after the restart before the
+ * real answer, and a doorbell the parked core never took would reach the
+ * new firmware before its own init. Both are read off without being
+ * delivered, at most a full FIFO each.
+ *
+ * The MIPS -> ARM side is read the way this driver always reads it. The
+ * ARM -> MIPS side is read at the address the MIPS reads it from (the
+ * doorbell register); that a read from the ARM pops it as well is not
+ * measured, which is why the line below says what is left. Nothing is read
+ * when a count is 0. How often either count is not 0 is not measured: the
+ * restarts of 08.10.2026 did not log them.
+ */
+void cpu_comm_msgbox_flush_mips(void)
+{
+	u32 tx, rx, n_tx = 0, n_rx = 0;
+
+	if (!msgbox_ctrl_base)
+		return;
+	tx = readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO);
+	rx = readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_RX_FIFO);
+	while (n_tx < H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO_DEPTH &&
+	       readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO)) {
+		readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_DATA);
+		n_tx++;
+	}
+	while (n_rx < H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO_DEPTH &&
+	       readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_RX_FIFO)) {
+		readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_RX_DATA);
+		n_rx++;
+	}
+	pr_info("cpu_comm: msgbox before the restart: ARM->MIPS %u word(s), %u read off, %u left; MIPS->ARM %u, %u read off, %u left\n",
+		tx, n_tx, n_tx ? readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_TX_FIFO) : tx,
+		rx, n_rx, n_rx ? readl(msgbox_ctrl_base + H713_MSGBOX_RX_FIFO) : rx);
+}
+
 /* Legacy stubs — no longer needed but keep exports for now */
 void cpu_comm_msgbox_probe_start(void) { }
 void cpu_comm_msgbox_probe_stop(void) { }
